# Google Drive sync. Optional: without it the app builds and runs exactly as
# before, and the Drive card on /backup stays a description with nothing to
# click.
#
# This is an OAuth *client id*, which is public by design — it ships in the
# bundle and is visible to anyone. **There is no client secret in the web flow,
# and one must never be added here.**
#
# The desktop build is the exception, and it is literally not this file — it is
# `.env.desktop.example`, copied to `.env.desktop.local`. Google's desktop
# client type does issue a secret, the main process reads it as
# MYTOME_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, and it never becomes a file in this repo.
# RFC 8252 §8.5 covers why a credential inside an installed application is not
# confidential in the first place.
#
# See docs/google-drive-sync.md for both clients: how to make them, which
# origins to authorize, and where each value goes.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) to use it in dev. Only the
# `VITE_`-prefixed line below belongs there — Vite exposes nothing else, and
# the desktop build reads its own `.env.desktop.local`, never this one.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
